INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_34',
  'A security team needs to capture all network traffic flowing between specific Amazon EC2 instances within a VPC for deep packet inspection and threat analysis. The solution must allow for centralized collection by a third-party appliance running on an EC2 instance in a different subnet, without impacting the performance of the application instances. Which AWS networking feature should a developer recommend to meet these requirements with minimal overhead?',
  'mcq',
  '["Configure VPC Flow Logs to export all traffic to Amazon CloudWatch Logs for analysis.","Implement Traffic Mirroring to send a copy of network traffic from the EC2 instances to a target Elastic Network Interface (ENI).","Deploy a custom packet capture agent on each EC2 instance to forward traffic to the analysis appliance.","Utilize AWS Network Firewall to inspect and forward traffic to the third-party appliance."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) is the most appropriate solution. Traffic Mirroring allows you to copy network traffic from an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) of an EC2 instance and send it to a target ENI for out-of-band inspection by security appliances. This provides deep packet visibility without impacting the performance of the mirrored instances. Option A (incorrect) VPC Flow Logs capture metadata about IP traffic (source/destination IP, ports, protocols, etc.) but do not capture the actual packet payload, which is required for deep packet inspection. Option C (incorrect) deploying custom agents on each EC2 instance would introduce significant operational overhead for deployment, management, and scaling, and could potentially impact instance performance. Option D (incorrect) AWS Network Firewall is primarily for stateful inspection and filtering of network traffic, not for mirroring raw packet data to a separate appliance for deep analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_35',
  'Which AWS service provides detailed metrics for virtually all AWS services, allowing for monitoring of resource utilization, application performance, and operational health, and enables setting alarms based on these metrics?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config","AWS X-Ray"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) Amazon CloudWatch is the primary monitoring and observability service for AWS. It collects monitoring and operational data in the form of logs, metrics, and events, and provides a unified view of AWS resources, applications, and services running on AWS and on-premises. It allows setting alarms based on metric thresholds. Option A (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail records API calls and related events made in your AWS account, primarily for auditing and governance, not for performance metrics or operational health. Option C (incorrect) AWS Config assesses, audits, and evaluates the configurations of your AWS resources, providing a configuration history and compliance checking. Option D (incorrect) AWS X-Ray helps developers analyze and debug distributed applications, providing end-to-end tracing of requests, but is not the primary service for general resource metrics and alarms.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_36',
  'A development team is deploying a new microservices application that requires real-time monitoring of custom application metrics, such as the number of user sign-ups per minute and API response times. The solution must be highly available and scalable, integrating seamlessly with existing AWS services for dashboards and alerting. Which AWS service should the developer use to ingest and visualize these custom metrics?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to stream metrics to Amazon S3 for later analysis.","AWS CloudTrail to log custom application events and then process them with AWS Lambda.","Amazon CloudWatch to publish custom metrics and create dashboards and alarms.","AWS X-Ray to trace individual requests and extract performance data."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) Amazon CloudWatch allows you to publish custom metrics from your applications using the PutMetricData API. These metrics can then be visualized on CloudWatch dashboards, and alarms can be set based on their values, providing a highly available and scalable solution for real-time monitoring. Option A (incorrect) Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is used for streaming data delivery to destinations like Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, or Splunk, which is more suited for raw log aggregation than real-time custom metric ingestion and visualization. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail logs API activity and events, not custom application metrics, and processing logs with AWS Lambda would add unnecessary complexity for simple metric ingestion. Option D (incorrect) AWS X-Ray is designed for distributed tracing of requests across microservices, which provides detailed request-level performance data, but it''s not the primary service for aggregating and visualizing custom application-level metrics over time.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_37',
  'A development team needs to monitor the health and performance of their Amazon EC2 instances, including CPU utilization, network I/O, and disk activity. They also need to set up alarms to be notified when certain thresholds are breached. Which AWS service is the most direct and efficient way to achieve this?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail for API activity logging.","Amazon CloudWatch for metrics and alarms.","AWS Config for resource configuration history.","AWS Systems Manager for operational insights."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) Amazon CloudWatch automatically collects basic metrics for Amazon EC2 instances, such as CPU utilization, network I/O, and disk activity. It also allows users to create custom dashboards and set alarms that trigger notifications when metric thresholds are crossed. Option A (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail records API calls and events in your AWS account, which is useful for security auditing and governance, but not for monitoring instance performance metrics. Option C (incorrect) AWS Config records configuration changes of AWS resources over time, which is important for compliance and troubleshooting configuration drift, but it does not provide real-time performance metrics or alarming capabilities. Option D (incorrect) AWS Systems Manager offers operational insights and automation for managing AWS resources, including EC2 instances, but it relies on CloudWatch for the underlying metrics and alarming functionality.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_38',
  'A company requires a solution to centralize the collection of logs from various AWS services, including AWS Lambda, Amazon S3, and Amazon EC2, for security auditing and operational troubleshooting. The solution must allow for long-term archival and easy querying. Which AWS service combination provides the most efficient and scalable approach?',
  'mcq',
  '["Send all logs directly to Amazon S3 for archival and use Amazon Athena for querying.","Configure AWS CloudTrail to capture all API calls and store them in Amazon S3.","Direct all logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, then export them to Amazon S3 for long-term archival and use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights for querying.","Utilize Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to stream logs to Amazon Redshift for analysis."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (correct) is the most efficient and scalable approach. Amazon CloudWatch Logs can collect logs from various AWS services. It provides a centralized repository, real-time monitoring, and CloudWatch Logs Insights for interactive querying. For long-term archival and cost-effectiveness, logs can be exported from CloudWatch Logs to Amazon S3. Option A (incorrect) while sending logs directly to Amazon S3 for archival is valid, it lacks the real-time monitoring and advanced querying capabilities that CloudWatch Logs offers natively without additional setup. Amazon Athena can query S3, but CloudWatch Logs provides a more integrated experience for operational logs. Option B (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail specifically captures API calls and related events, not all types of application or service logs (e.g., Lambda function logs, S3 access logs, EC2 instance logs). It''s a component of a logging strategy but not a comprehensive solution for all log types. Option D (incorrect) Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose can stream logs, but Amazon Redshift is a data warehouse optimized for analytical queries on structured data, which might be overkill and more expensive for general log storage and querying compared to CloudWatch Logs and S3.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_4_39',
  'A developer needs to establish a baseline for network performance and identify unusual traffic spikes or drops within their VPC. They want to visualize network activity and set up alerts for anomalies. Which AWS service combination should be used to achieve this effectively?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudTrail to monitor network API calls and Amazon SNS for notifications.","VPC Flow Logs published to Amazon CloudWatch Logs, with CloudWatch Metrics and Alarms configured.","AWS Config to track network resource changes and AWS Systems Manager for operational data.","Amazon GuardDuty for threat detection and AWS Security Hub for compliance checks."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (correct) VPC Flow Logs capture metadata about IP traffic, which can be published to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. From CloudWatch Logs, metrics can be extracted (e.g., bytes transferred, packet counts) and visualized in CloudWatch Dashboards. CloudWatch Alarms can then be configured on these metrics to detect unusual spikes or drops, providing an effective solution for baselining network performance and anomaly detection. Option A (incorrect) AWS CloudTrail monitors API calls related to network resources, but it does not provide the granular traffic flow data needed to establish performance baselines or detect traffic anomalies. Amazon SNS is for notifications, but it needs a source for the alerts. Option C (incorrect) AWS Config tracks configuration changes of network resources, which is important for governance but not for monitoring real-time traffic performance. AWS Systems Manager provides operational data but doesn''t natively capture network flow data for this purpose. Option D (incorrect) Amazon GuardDuty is a threat detection service that analyzes various data sources, including VPC Flow Logs, but its primary role is security threat detection, not general network performance baselining and anomaly detection for traffic patterns. AWS Security Hub aggregates security findings.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_4',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

