  '{0,1}',
  'To achieve high availability with AWS Direct Connect, it is recommended to use multiple Direct Connect locations (Option A) to protect against failures at a single location. Additionally, establishing multiple Direct Connect connections (Option B) within the same or different locations provides redundancy. AWS Transit Gateway (Option C) can centralize connectivity but doesn''t inherently make the Direct Connect link itself highly available. Amazon Route 53 (Option D) and AWS Global Accelerator (Option E) are for DNS and global traffic management, respectively, not for the underlying Direct Connect link''s availability.',
