  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_25',
  'A company requires a highly available and resilient connection between their on-premises data center and AWS. Which design principles and services should be considered to achieve this goal? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Utilize multiple AWS Direct Connect connections from different locations.","Implement a single AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection as the primary link.","Configure AWS Direct Connect with a single virtual interface.","Deploy multiple AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections over diverse internet paths.","Use Amazon SQS for inter-region communication."]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (Utilize multiple AWS Direct Connect connections from different locations) provides redundancy and resilience by preventing a single point of failure at a physical location. Option D (Deploy multiple AWS Site-to-Site VPN connections over diverse internet paths) offers a highly available and resilient backup or primary connection by leveraging different internet service providers and network paths. Option B (Implement a single AWS Site-to-Site VPN connection as the primary link) introduces a single point of failure and does not meet high availability requirements. Option C (Configure AWS Direct Connect with a single virtual interface) also creates a single point of failure at the virtual interface level. Option E (Use Amazon SQS for inter-region communication) is a messaging service and not relevant to establishing network connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_26',
  'A solutions architect needs to extend an on-premises network to AWS securely and efficiently. Which AWS services facilitate this extension by creating secure tunnels or dedicated connections? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Direct Connect","AWS Site-to-Site VPN","Amazon VPC","AWS Global Accelerator","Amazon Route 53"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated, private network connection from your premises to AWS, bypassing the public internet. Option B (AWS Site-to-Site VPN) creates an encrypted tunnel over the public internet, securely connecting your on-premises network to your AWS VPC. Option C (Amazon VPC) is the fundamental networking service in AWS but doesn''t, by itself, extend on-premises networks. Option D (AWS Global Accelerator) improves application availability and performance using the AWS global network, but it''s not for extending private networks. Option E (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_27',
  'A company is implementing a hybrid cloud architecture and wants to share their AWS Direct Connect gateway with multiple AWS accounts within their organization. Which AWS service enables this resource sharing? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)","AWS Organizations","AWS Transit Gateway","AWS PrivateLink","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) allows you to share AWS resources, including Direct Connect gateways and Transit Gateways, with other AWS accounts or within your AWS Organization. Option C (AWS Transit Gateway) can be attached to a Direct Connect gateway, and then VPCs from multiple accounts can connect to the Transit Gateway, effectively sharing the Direct Connect connection. Option B (AWS Organizations) helps manage multiple AWS accounts but doesn''t directly share network resources; it works in conjunction with RAM. Option D (AWS PrivateLink) provides private connectivity to services, not for sharing network gateways. Option E (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational insights and management, not network resource sharing.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_28',
  'A company operates a hybrid cloud environment with critical on-premises applications that need to securely communicate with services hosted in an AWS VPC. The network team requires a highly available and resilient connection with predictable performance and the ability to control routing paths using standard routing protocols. Which two AWS services or features are essential for establishing this robust connectivity? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Site-to-Site VPN","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon Route 53 Resolver","Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)","AWS Transit Gateway"]'::json,
  '{1,3}',
  'Option B (AWS Direct Connect) provides a dedicated network connection from an on-premises network to AWS, offering consistent network performance and reduced bandwidth costs compared to internet-based VPNs. This is crucial for predictable performance. Option D (Border Gateway Protocol (BGP)) is the routing protocol used with Direct Connect (and VPN) to exchange routing information between the on-premises network and AWS, enabling dynamic routing and control over traffic paths. Option A (AWS Site-to-Site VPN) offers secure connectivity over the public internet, but lacks the predictable performance of Direct Connect. Option C (Amazon Route 53 Resolver) is for DNS resolution, not network connectivity itself. Option E (AWS Transit Gateway) can aggregate multiple VPN or Direct Connect connections, but BGP is still required for routing, and Direct Connect is the underlying physical connection for predictable performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_29',
  'A large enterprise is migrating a complex application suite to AWS, requiring seamless and secure connectivity between their on-premises data centers and multiple AWS VPCs across different AWS accounts. They need to ensure high availability and efficient routing for thousands of IP prefixes, while also enabling centralized network management. Which two networking components are critical for this hybrid architecture? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["VPC Peering","AWS Direct Connect Gateway","AWS Transit Gateway","Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)","AWS Client VPN"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (AWS Direct Connect Gateway) allows a single Direct Connect connection to connect to multiple VPCs across different AWS accounts and AWS Regions, simplifying connectivity for large enterprises. Option C (AWS Transit Gateway) acts as a central hub for connecting VPCs and on-premises networks, enabling a hub-and-spoke architecture that simplifies routing, enhances scalability, and facilitates centralized network management across many VPCs and accounts. Option A (VPC Peering) is limited to connecting two VPCs at a time and does not scale well for thousands of prefixes or multi-account scenarios. Option D (Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)) is the fundamental building block for isolated networks in AWS, but it doesn''t provide the inter-VPC or hybrid connectivity solution itself. Option E (AWS Client VPN) is for remote access for individual users, not for site-to-site connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_50_m_50_5_30',
  'An organization is building a hybrid cloud architecture and needs to extend their on-premises Active Directory to AWS for seamless user authentication and authorization. They also require a secure and private network connection to AWS, and the ability to share network resources like a Transit Gateway across multiple AWS accounts. Which two AWS services or features are crucial for enabling this integrated hybrid environment? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Directory Service","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon Route 53 Resolver Endpoints","AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)","AWS Client VPN"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (AWS Directory Service) allows extending an on-premises Active Directory to AWS, providing managed domain controllers that can be used for authentication and authorization for AWS resources and applications. Option D (AWS Resource Access Manager (RAM)) enables sharing of AWS resources, such as AWS Transit Gateways, across different AWS accounts, which is vital for a centralized hybrid network strategy. Option B (AWS Direct Connect) provides the private network connection, but RAM and Directory Service are specifically for sharing and identity. Option C (Amazon Route 53 Resolver Endpoints) is for hybrid DNS resolution, which is often used in conjunction with Directory Service but is not the primary service for identity or resource sharing. Option E (AWS Client VPN) is for remote access for individual users, not for extending Active Directory or sharing network resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_50_5',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

