  'Match each CloudWatch component to its main function.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"CloudWatch Alarms","B":"CloudWatch Dashboards","C":"CloudWatch Events"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'CloudWatch Alarms (left[0]) watch a single metric or the result of a math expression based on multiple metrics and perform one or more actions based on the value of the metric or expression relative to a threshold over a number of time periods. CloudWatch Dashboards (left[1]) are customizable home pages in the CloudWatch console that you can use to monitor your resources in a single view, even across different Regions. CloudWatch Events (left[2]), now Amazon EventBridge, delivers a near real-time stream of system events that describe changes in AWS resources, allowing you to set up rules to match events and route them to one or more target functions or streams.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain50_11',
  NOW(),
  2,
  '{"left":["CloudWatch Alarms","CloudWatch Dashboards","CloudWatch Events"],"right":["Notifies on metric thresholds","Visualizes metrics and logs","Triggers actions on changes"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_50_4',
  'easy'
);

