  'Match the AWS service to its role in collecting access logs for applications.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon S3 Access Logs","B":"Elastic Load Balancing Access Logs","C":"Amazon CloudFront Access Logs"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Amazon S3 Access Logs (left[0]) record all requests made to an S3 bucket, providing details about the request, requester, and outcome. Elastic Load Balancing Access Logs (left[1]) capture detailed information about requests sent to your Application Load Balancers or Network Load Balancers, including client IP, latency, and request path. Amazon CloudFront Access Logs (left[2]) log all viewer requests for content delivered by a CloudFront distribution, including information about the request, the viewer, and the response.',
