  'Match each Amazon Route 53 routing policy to its traffic management behavior.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Weighted Routing","B":"Failover Routing","C":"Multivalue Answer Routing"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Weighted Routing (left item 0) allows you to distribute traffic to multiple resources based on specified weights. Failover Routing (left item 1) automatically routes traffic to a healthy resource when the primary resource becomes unhealthy. Multivalue Answer Routing (left item 2) returns up to eight healthy records, allowing clients to make their own choice of which resource to use, which can improve availability.',
