  'A Route 53 Resolver Inbound Endpoint (left item 0) allows DNS queries from on-premises networks to be resolved by the Route 53 Resolver in your VPC for AWS resources. An Outbound Endpoint (left item 1) enables DNS queries originating from your VPC to be forwarded to on-premises DNS servers. Resolver Rules (left item 2) define the conditional forwarding logic, specifying which domain names should be resolved by which DNS servers.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain51_11',
  NOW(),
  28,
  '{"left":["Inbound Endpoint","Outbound Endpoint","Resolver Rules"],"right":["Resolve on-premises queries for AWS","Resolve AWS queries for on-premises","Define conditional forwarding logic"]}'::json,
