  '["To control inbound and outbound traffic for subnets.","To act as a virtual firewall for Amazon EC2 instances.","To provide network address translation (NAT) for private subnets.","To manage routing tables for network traffic within a VPC."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (To act as a virtual firewall for Amazon EC2 instances) accurately describes the primary function of an Amazon VPC security group. Security groups operate at the instance level and control traffic to and from individual EC2 instances. Option A describes Network Access Control Lists (NACLs), which operate at the subnet level. Option C describes a NAT Gateway or NAT instance. Option D describes VPC route tables.',
