  '{0}',
  'Option A (To control inbound and outbound traffic at the subnet level) is the correct purpose of a Network Access Control List (NACL). NACLs are stateless firewalls that apply to all instances within a subnet. Option B describes security groups, which are stateful and operate at the instance level. Option C describes Amazon Route 53 Resolver. Option D describes AWS Network Firewall.',
