  'Match the AWS networking concept to its description for routing stability.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Route Summarization","B":"Longest Prefix Match","C":"Static Route"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Route Summarization (or aggregation) is the process of combining multiple routes into a single, more general route, reducing the size of routing tables. Longest Prefix Match is the rule that states if a packet''s destination IP address matches multiple routes in the routing table, the route with the most specific (longest) prefix is chosen. A Static Route is a manually configured entry in a route table that specifies a path for network traffic.',
