  NULL,
  'Border Gateway Protocol (BGP) (left: 0) is used to dynamically exchange routing information between autonomous systems, suitable for managing thousands of IP prefixes in complex networks. Static Routes (left: 1) involve manual route entries for specific destinations, which can be less scalable for large, dynamic environments. AWS Site-to-Site VPN (left: 2) establishes an encrypted tunnel over the public internet, providing secure but potentially variable performance. A Direct Connect Link Aggregation Group (LAG) (left: 3) bundles multiple physical Direct Connect connections to achieve higher bandwidth and increased resilience.',
