  NULL,
  'VPC Peering (left: 0) creates a direct, private network connection between two VPCs, allowing instances to communicate as if they are in the same network. AWS PrivateLink (left: 1) provides private access to supported AWS services from a VPC, keeping traffic within the AWS network. A Transit Gateway Route Table (left: 2) is used to control traffic flow through a central Transit Gateway hub, enabling complex routing policies. A Gateway VPC Endpoint (left: 3) specifically provides private access to Amazon S3 and Amazon DynamoDB from a VPC, without requiring an Internet Gateway.',
