  NULL,
  'A Network Access Control List (NACL) (left: 0) provides stateless subnet-level traffic filtering, evaluating all inbound and outbound rules independently. A Security Group (left: 1) offers stateful instance-level traffic filtering, remembering the state of connections and automatically allowing return traffic. VPC Flow Logs (left: 2) capture IP traffic information for a VPC''s network interfaces, useful for monitoring and troubleshooting. A Route Table (left: 3) directs network traffic between subnets and various gateways, determining where traffic is sent.',
