  'm_52_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_52_m_52_2_109',
  'A security team needs to inspect all inbound and outbound network traffic for a specific Amazon EC2 instance for deep packet inspection and threat analysis. Match the AWS service to the capability that best supports this requirement.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Traffic Mirroring","B":"VPC Flow Logs","C":"AWS CloudWatch Metrics"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Traffic Mirroring (left item 0) is the most suitable service for deep packet inspection as it allows duplicating actual network traffic from an EC2 instance''s Elastic Network Interface (ENI) to a security appliance. VPC Flow Logs (left item 1) provide metadata about IP traffic flows (source/destination IP, port, protocol, action) but not the packet content itself. AWS CloudWatch Metrics (left item 2) provide aggregated performance data, not detailed traffic content.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain52_11',
  NOW(),
  32,
  '{"left":["Traffic Mirroring","VPC Flow Logs","AWS CloudWatch Metrics"],"right":["Duplicates network traffic to an analysis appliance","Records metadata about IP traffic","Provides aggregated performance data"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_52_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_52_m_52_2_110',
  'Match common network troubleshooting concepts to their descriptions.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Packet Loss","B":"MTU Issues","C":"Misconfiguration"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Packet Loss (left item 0) occurs when one or more packets of data traveling across a computer network fail to reach their destination. MTU Issues (left item 1) arise when the Maximum Transmission Unit (MTU) size is incorrectly set, leading to fragmentation or dropped packets. Misconfiguration (left item 2) refers to errors in network settings, such as incorrect route table entries, security group rules, or network ACLs, which can prevent proper connectivity.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain52_11',
  NOW(),
  33,
  '{"left":["Packet Loss","MTU Issues","Misconfiguration"],"right":["Data packets failing to reach their destination","Incorrect Maximum Transmission Unit settings","Incorrectly set up network settings or rules"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_52_2',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_52_m_52_2_111',
  'A company is experiencing intermittent connectivity issues with its microservices deployed in a VPC. The operations team needs to diagnose the root cause, which could involve misconfigured security groups, routing problems, or network ACLs. They require tools to capture and analyze network traffic and verify network paths.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"VPC Flow Logs","B":"AWS CloudWatch Logs","C":"AWS Network Manager","D":"AWS Reachability Analyzer"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'VPC Flow Logs (left: 0) record IP traffic information for network interfaces within a VPC, providing crucial data for troubleshooting connectivity issues. AWS CloudWatch Logs (left: 1) is a centralized logging service that can ingest and store logs from various applications and AWS services, including Flow Logs. AWS Network Manager (left: 2) offers central management and operational visibility for global networks, including AWS and on-premises components. AWS Reachability Analyzer (left: 3) analyzes network configurations to determine if a specific path between two resources is reachable and identifies any blocking components.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain52_11',
  NOW(),
  34,
  '{"left":["VPC Flow Logs","AWS CloudWatch Logs","AWS Network Manager","AWS Reachability Analyzer"],"right":["Records IP traffic information for VPC interfaces.","Centralized logging service for applications and AWS services.","Central management for global networks across AWS and on-premises.","Analyzes network configurations to determine path reachability."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_52_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_52_m_52_2_112',
  'A security team needs to monitor and inspect network traffic within a VPC for suspicious activity and compliance auditing. They require a mechanism to capture and forward specific traffic to security appliances for deep packet inspection without impacting the production workload.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"VPC Traffic Mirroring","B":"AWS Security Hub","C":"Amazon GuardDuty","D":"AWS WAF"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'VPC Traffic Mirroring (left: 0) allows copying network traffic from an Elastic Network Interface (ENI) to a monitoring destination, such as a security appliance, for deep packet inspection. AWS Security Hub (left: 1) provides a centralized view of security alerts and compliance status across multiple AWS accounts. Amazon GuardDuty (left: 2) is a threat detection service that continuously monitors for malicious activity and unauthorized behavior in AWS accounts and workloads. AWS WAF (left: 3) protects web applications from common web exploits that could affect application availability, compromise security, or consume excessive resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain52_11',
  NOW(),
  35,
  '{"left":["VPC Traffic Mirroring","AWS Security Hub","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS WAF"],"right":["Copies network traffic to a monitoring destination.","Centralized view of security alerts and compliance status.","Threat detection service for AWS accounts and workloads.","Protects web applications from common web exploits."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_52_2',
  'hard'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_52_m_52_2_113',
  'A DevOps team is responsible for maintaining network connectivity for a complex application deployed across multiple VPCs and AWS Regions. They need to automate checks for common network misconfigurations and ensure that network changes do not inadvertently break existing connectivity.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS Config Rules","B":"AWS Systems Manager Automation","C":"AWS CloudFormation","D":"AWS CloudTrail"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS Config Rules (left: 0) continuously evaluate AWS resource configurations against desired settings, helping to identify network misconfigurations. AWS Systems Manager Automation (left: 1) allows for the automation of operational tasks across AWS resources, including network-related checks and remediation. AWS CloudFormation (left: 2) is an Infrastructure as Code service used for provisioning and managing AWS resources, ensuring consistent deployments. AWS CloudTrail (left: 3) logs API calls and events made in an AWS account, providing an audit trail for governance, compliance, and operational troubleshooting.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain52_11',
  NOW(),
  36,
  '{"left":["AWS Config Rules","AWS Systems Manager Automation","AWS CloudFormation","AWS CloudTrail"],"right":["Evaluates AWS resource configurations against desired settings.","Automates operational tasks across AWS resources.","Infrastructure as Code service for provisioning AWS resources.","Logs API calls and events for governance, compliance, and auditing."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_52_2',
  'hard'
);

