INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_80',
  'When configuring Amazon VPC endpoints for private access to AWS services, which mechanisms can be used to control access to the endpoint? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Endpoint policies","Network Access Control Lists (NACLs)","Security Groups","AWS WAF","AWS Shield"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Endpoint policies) are IAM resource policies that you attach to an interface endpoint to control which IAM principals can use the endpoint and what actions they can perform. Option C (Security Groups) associated with the endpoint network interfaces or the requesting instances can control network traffic to and from the endpoint. Option B (Network Access Control Lists - NACLs) can also apply at the subnet level where the endpoint is located, but Security Groups offer more granular control specific to the endpoint. Option D (AWS WAF) and Option E (AWS Shield) are for web application and DDoS protection, respectively, not for controlling access to VPC endpoints.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  40,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_81',
  'A company requires a centralized ingress and egress point for all traffic entering and leaving their AWS environment to enforce consistent security policies. They plan to use a dedicated ''perimeter VPC'' for this purpose. Which AWS network security components are essential to implement within this perimeter VPC to filter and inspect traffic? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Network Firewall","AWS WAF","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon S3","AWS Certificate Manager"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Network Firewall) provides deep packet inspection, intrusion prevention, and web filtering capabilities, making it ideal for inspecting all traffic flowing through a perimeter VPC. Option B (AWS WAF) is crucial for protecting web applications and APIs that might be exposed through the perimeter VPC (e.g., via an Application Load Balancer). Option C (Amazon CloudFront) is a content delivery network. Option D (Amazon S3) is an object storage service. Option E (AWS Certificate Manager) is for managing SSL/TLS certificates.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  41,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_82',
  'Which AWS services offer capabilities to protect against Distributed Denial of Service (DDoS) attacks? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon GuardDuty","AWS Shield","AWS WAF","Amazon Inspector","Amazon VPC"]'::json,
  '{1,2}',
  'Option B (AWS Shield) is a managed DDoS protection service that safeguards applications running on AWS. It provides always-on detection and automatic inline mitigations. Option C (AWS WAF - Web Application Firewall) can help mitigate certain types of DDoS attacks, particularly those targeting the application layer (Layer 7). Option A (Amazon GuardDuty) is a threat detection service, not primarily for DDoS protection. Option D (Amazon Inspector) is a vulnerability management service. Option E (Amazon VPC) is the networking foundation, not a DDoS protection service itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  42,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'medium'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_83',
  'Within an Amazon VPC, which network security features allow for granular control over traffic based on IP addresses, ports, and protocols at both the subnet and instance levels? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Network Access Control Lists (NACLs)","AWS Network Firewall","Security Groups","Amazon Route 53","AWS Transit Gateway"]'::json,
  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Network Access Control Lists - NACLs) provide stateless packet filtering at the subnet level, allowing or denying traffic based on IP addresses, ports, and protocols. Option C (Security Groups) provide stateful packet filtering at the instance level, controlling inbound and outbound traffic for EC2 instances based on IP addresses, ports, and protocols. Option B (AWS Network Firewall) is a managed firewall service that operates at the VPC level. Option D (Amazon Route 53) is a DNS service. Option E (AWS Transit Gateway) connects VPCs and on-premises networks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  43,
