  '{0,2,3,1}',
  'Establishing a Site-to-Site VPN connection begins by defining the on-premises side to AWS, which involves creating a Customer Gateway (CGW) in AWS with the public IP of the on-premises VPN device (Option A). Next, a Virtual Private Gateway (VGW) is created and attached to the AWS VPC, serving as the VPN concentrator on the AWS side (Option C). With both gateways defined, a Site-to-Site VPN connection is then created in AWS, linking the VGW and CGW (Option D). The final step is to configure the on-premises VPN device using the configuration details provided by AWS for the newly created VPN connection (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
