  'To enforce HTTPS on CloudFront, the first step is to obtain an SSL/TLS certificate for your custom domain using AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) (Option B). Next, you create a CloudFront web distribution, specifying the Amazon S3 bucket as the origin (Option C). After the distribution is created, you configure its ''Viewer Protocol Policy'' to ''Redirect HTTP to HTTPS'' or ''HTTPS Only'' to ensure all viewer traffic is encrypted (Option A). Finally, you update your DNS records (e.g., in Amazon Route 53) to point your custom domain to the CloudFront distribution''s domain name (Option D).',
