INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_87',
  'A developer needs to restrict inbound traffic to an Amazon EC2 instance to only specific IP addresses and ports. Arrange the following steps to configure a Security Group for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Add inbound rules to the Security Group specifying allowed protocols, ports, and source IP addresses.","Create a new Security Group in the Amazon VPC console.","Associate the Security Group with the target EC2 instance.","Give the Security Group a name and description, and select the VPC."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'To restrict inbound traffic, you first create a new Security Group in the Amazon VPC console (Option B). Next, you give it a name, description, and select the VPC it belongs to (Option D). After creation, you add inbound rules (Option A) to specify which protocols, ports, and source IP addresses are allowed. Finally, you associate this Security Group with your EC2 instance (Option C) to apply the rules.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_88',
  'A network administrator wants to block all inbound HTTP traffic to a subnet, except for specific management IPs, using a Network ACL. Arrange the following steps to configure the Network ACL.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new Network ACL and associate it with the target subnet.","Add an inbound DENY rule for HTTP (port 80) from all IP addresses (0.0.0.0/0) with a high rule number.","Add an inbound ALLOW rule for HTTP (port 80) from the specific management IP addresses with a low rule number.","Ensure the Network ACL has an implicit DENY rule at the end."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To block HTTP traffic selectively, first create a new Network ACL and associate it with the target subnet (Option A). Next, add an inbound ALLOW rule for HTTP from your specific management IP addresses with a low rule number (Option C), as NACLs process rules in numerical order. Then, add an inbound DENY rule for HTTP from all IP addresses with a higher rule number (Option B) to block all other HTTP traffic. The implicit DENY rule (Option D) is always present at the end of every NACL and will catch any traffic not explicitly allowed or denied by previous rules.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  23,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_89',
  'A developer needs to allow an EC2 instance in a private subnet to securely access Amazon S3 without traversing the public internet. Arrange the following steps to create a VPC Gateway Endpoint for Amazon S3.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new VPC Gateway Endpoint for Amazon S3 in the VPC console.","Select the VPC where the EC2 instance resides.","Add a route to the VPC''s route table(s) that points S3 traffic to the Gateway Endpoint.","Choose the specific S3 service and select the route tables for your private subnets."]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}',
  'To create a VPC Gateway Endpoint for Amazon S3, you first create a new Gateway Endpoint in the VPC console (Option A). Next, you select the VPC where your EC2 instance resides (Option B). Then, you choose the S3 service and specify the route tables associated with your private subnets (Option D) to allow them to use the endpoint. Finally, a route is automatically added to the selected route tables (Option C) directing S3 traffic through the endpoint.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  24,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_90',
  'A security engineer needs to deploy a centralized network firewall within a VPC to inspect all inbound and outbound traffic. Arrange the following steps to configure a basic AWS Network Firewall policy.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new firewall policy in the AWS Network Firewall console.","Define stateful and stateless rule groups within the policy.","Associate the firewall policy with an AWS Network Firewall resource.","Configure the default action for stateless and stateful rule groups."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}',
  'To configure an AWS Network Firewall policy, you first create a new firewall policy in the AWS Network Firewall console (Option A). Next, you configure the default action for both stateless and stateful rule groups (Option D), which determines how traffic is handled if no specific rules match. Then, you define your specific stateful and stateless rule groups (Option B) to inspect traffic. Finally, you associate this firewall policy with an AWS Network Firewall resource (Option C) that is deployed in your VPC.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  25,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_91',
  'A developer needs to set up a new VPC with public and private subnets to host a web application. Arrange the following steps to create this basic VPC architecture.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Internet Gateway and attach it to the VPC.","Create a new VPC with a specified CIDR block.","Create public and private subnets within the VPC.","Configure route tables for public and private subnets, associating the public route table with the Internet Gateway."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'The foundational step is to create a new VPC with its CIDR block (Option B). Next, you create an Internet Gateway and attach it to the VPC (Option A) to enable internet connectivity. Then, you create your public and private subnets within the VPC (Option C). Finally, you configure separate route tables for these subnets, ensuring the public route table has a route to the Internet Gateway (Option D) for outbound internet access.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  26,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_92',
  'A security engineer identifies a malicious IP address range and needs to block all traffic from it at the subnet level. Arrange the following steps to use a Network ACL to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new Network ACL or select an existing one associated with the target subnet.","Add an inbound DENY rule for the malicious IP address range (e.g., 192.0.2.0/24) with a low rule number.","Verify the Network ACL is explicitly associated with the subnet(s) to be protected.","Ensure there are no conflicting ALLOW rules with a lower rule number that would permit traffic from the malicious range."]'::json,
  '{0,1,3,2}',
  'To block a malicious IP range, first create a new Network ACL or select an existing one associated with the target subnet (Option A). Next, add an inbound DENY rule for the malicious IP range with a low rule number (Option B), ensuring it''s processed early. It''s crucial to ensure there are no conflicting ALLOW rules with a lower rule number (Option D) that would override the DENY. Finally, verify the Network ACL is correctly associated with the target subnet(s) (Option C) to apply the blocking rule.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain53_11',
  NOW(),
  27,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_53_1',
  'easy'
);

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_53_m_53_1_93',
  'A developer needs to create a Security Group that allows only SSH access from their office IP address. Arrange the following steps to configure this Security Group.',
