  '{0,2,1,3}',
  'To configure a Security Group for restricted SSH access, you first create a new Security Group (Option A). Next, you add an inbound rule (Option C) to define what traffic is allowed. Then, you specify the rule details: Type SSH, Protocol TCP, Port Range 22 (Option B). Finally, you set the source for this rule to your office''s specific public IP address range (Option D) to limit access.',
