  '{1,0,2,3}',
  'To configure a security group for inbound SSH access, you first navigate to the EC2 console and select ''Security Groups'' (Option B). Then, you select the specific security group that is associated with your EC2 instance (Option A). Within the security group settings, you add a new inbound rule, specifying SSH (port 22) as the type and entering the allowed source IP address range (Option C). Finally, you save the new inbound rule to apply the changes to the security group (Option D).',
