  NULL,
  'TLS (Transport Layer Security) (left[0]) is widely used to secure communication over web protocols like HTTPS, ensuring data confidentiality and integrity (right[0]). IPsec (Internet Protocol Security) (left[1]) is a suite of protocols that provides secure communication over IP networks, commonly used for VPN connections (right[1]). DNSSEC (Domain Name System Security Extensions) (left[2]) adds security to the DNS protocol by digitally signing DNS records to prevent spoofing and ensure authenticity (right[2]).',
